	Example : 3 
	===============
		 ACID Properties – Cart & Payment Intent Example
		Scenario (Project Flow)
	
		First, cart is created
	
		Then payment intent is created (mandatory before payment)
	
		Customer updates cart (like increasing quantity)
	
		System recalculates total amount
	
		Payment intent, cart, and cart details tables are updated
	
		1️⃣ Atomicity
		--------------
		Atomicity means all steps must succeed or none should happen.
	
		In our project:
	
		When customer updates the cart:
	
		Update cart total
	
		Update cart details
	
		Update payment intent amount
	
		👉 If payment intent update fails, then:
	
		Cart update is rolled back
	
		Cart details update is rolled back
	
		So partial update never happens.
	
		Cart and payment intent are always updated together.
	
		2️⃣ Consistency
		----------------
		Consistency means business rules must be correct before and after transaction.
	
		In our project:
	
		Cart total amount = Payment intent amount
	
		Cart details prices = Cart total
	
		No mismatch allowed like:
	
		Cart amount updated but payment intent old ❌
	
		Payment intent updated but cart old ❌
	
		Database always moves from correct state to correct state.
	
		3️⃣ Isolation
		----------------
		Isolation means multiple updates do not disturb each other.
	
		In our project:
	
		User updates quantity
	
		At same time, user refreshes page or adds another item
	
		Only one transaction works at a time for the cart.
		Other update waits.
	
		This avoids wrong price calculation and duplicate updates.
	
		4️⃣ Durability
		--------------
		Durability means once update is completed, data is permanently saved.
	
		In our project:
	
		Cart updated
	
		Payment intent updated
	
		Transaction committed
	
		Even if server crashes, after restart:
	
		Cart has latest price
	
		Payment intent has latest amount
	
		Data is not lost.
	
	
	
	